reel	probe — 自动备料写 spec 草稿	2026-10-04T14:18:43.1913534Z         "excerpts": [
reel	probe — 自动备料写 spec 草稿	2026-10-04T14:18:43.1917352Z           "“I had a terrible start. Two double faults at the beginning. It was quite cold and honestly, I didn’t feel warmed up, but my fault,” Djokovic said. “I gave him an early break and then it was hard to come back in the first set. I had a couple of break points when he was serving for the set at 5-4, but didn’t use them, but I kind of felt already from midway through the first set that I was starting to get a good rhythm, at least one my serve and on serve plus one.”",
reel	probe — 自动备料写 spec 草稿	2026-10-04T14:18:43.1924117Z           "Djokovic was made to pay for a slow start to what was an ultimately hard-fought opening set on Beijing’s stadium court, where Zverev expertly capitalised on a sloppy few opening points from his opponent to break serve in the first game. From there, Djokovic rapidly upped his level and, after saving a set point to hold serve for 4-5, he carved out his first break points of the match at 15/40 in the next game."
